| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary indigo | `#4338CA` | Main actions, active navigation, links |
| Primary hover | `#3730A3` | Hover state for primary actions |
| Primary dark | `#312E81` | Strong emphasis when needed |
| Text primary | `#111827` | Headings and main body text |
| Text secondary | `#4B5563` | Descriptions, secondary labels |
| Border grey | `#D1D5DB` | Inputs, dividers, card outlines |
| Page background | `#F9FAFB` | Page canvas |
| Surface | `#FFFFFF` | Cards, forms, dialogs, sidebar |
| Success | `#15803D` | Completed operations and confirmation |
| Warning | `#B45309` | Incomplete profiles and caution messages |
| Error | `#B91C1C` | Failed operations and validation errors |


## 3. Typography

**Decision: Inter**, with the fallback stack `Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif`.

- Page titles: 24 px, weight 600.
- Section titles: 18–20 px, weight 600.
- Body text: 16 px, weight 400.
- Labels, helper text, and table metadata: 14 px, weight 400–500.
- Keep terminology and capitalization consistent: **Student**, **Profile**, **Formation**, **Group**, **Skill**, and **Onboarding**.

## 4. Application shell and navigation

After login, **Admin** and **Teacher** use a shared application shell: left sidebar, top bar with page title, current user/role and logout, and a main content area. On narrow screens the sidebar becomes an accessible menu drawer. **Student** uses the same visual shell with a smaller, student-specific navigation menu.

- The current route is highlighted in the sidebar.
- Each screen has one clear heading and consistent spacing.
- Use descriptive names (for example, **Programming 1**, not **Unit #3**).
- Hide navigation entries for unauthorized roles. Independently enforce permissions in route guards and in the backend.
- Never show a sidebar link to an unimplemented or disabled screen.
- After login, send Admin and Teacher to `/dashboard`; send Student to `/me/onboarding` if first-login onboarding is required, otherwise `/me/profile`.

### Sidebar by role

| Role | Sidebar items and destinations |
| --- | --- |
| **Admin** | Dashboard (`/dashboard`); Users (`/admin/users`); Students (`/students`); Courses (`/admin/courses`); Course units (`/admin/course-units`); Academic records (`/admin/academic-records`); Formations (`/formations`) |
| **Teacher** | Dashboard (`/dashboard`); Students (`/students`); Formations (`/formations`) |
| **Student** | My profile (`/me/profile`); My history (`/me/history`); My goals (`/me/goals`); My portfolio (`/me/portfolio`) |

The Admin course, course-unit, and academic-record links are shown only if their corresponding Sprint 2 screens exist. Student goals and portfolio links appear only after their optional features are implemented. **Onboarding is a guided flow, not a permanent sidebar item.** Creating a formation is an action on the Formations screen, not a separate permanent sidebar item.

