## 6. Shared interface rules

All screens must follow the backlog's quality standard:

- Provide **loading, empty, error and success** states.
- Validate forms before submission and show backend errors in plain language.
- Use consistent buttons, labels, spacing and confirmation dialogs.
- Support both **360 px** and **1280 px** viewport widths.
- Associate labels with inputs, provide visible keyboard focus and support keyboard navigation.
- Never show internal database IDs as user facing labels; avoid dead links and browser console errors.
- Confirm consequential actions and provide feedback after save, delete, or formation changes.

## 7. Approval and implementation guidance

This document defines the intended **design and navigation decisions**. F1 will implement the MUI theme/component foundation; F2 will implement the shared shell; A6/A7 will implement login, guards and role-aware navigation. Other screens will reuse these decisions.


